## Summary

Since `@adobe/react-spectrum@3.47.2`, the prebuilt CSS in `dist/private/*.css` contains **native CSS nesting** (`& { … }`). In `3.47.1` the same rules shipped flat. Native nesting requires Chrome 112+ / Safari 16.5+ / Firefox 117+. On any older engine the parser discards the nested block, so the rule collapses to empty and the component renders unstyled — for icons this drops `inline-size`/`block-size`, and the SVG expands to fill its container.

This is a **patch-level** change to published artifacts that silently raised the effective CSS browser floor to Chrome 112, below `react-spectrum`'s own declared support baseline.

<img width="1824" height="652" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/96ee21a9-f548-4762-bce4-3ed8e4d9b664" />
> **Visual:** a `size="S"` workflow icon rendering at ~18px (3.47.1, flat) vs. ~429px (3.47.2, parsed by an engine without native nesting).

## Regression — `dist/private/icon_vars.css`, rule `.spectrum-Icon--sizeS`

```css
/* 3.47.1 — flat, portable (works everywhere) */
.…spectrum-Icon--sizeS, .…spectrum-Icon--sizeS img, .…spectrum-Icon--sizeS svg {
  block-size: var(--spectrum-alias-workflow-icon-size, …);
  inline-size: var(--spectrum-alias-workflow-icon-size, …);
}

/* 3.47.2 — native nesting (needs Chrome ≥112 / Safari ≥16.5 / Firefox ≥117) */
.…spectrum-Icon--sizeS {
  &, & img, & svg {
    block-size: var(--spectrum-alias-workflow-icon-size, …);
    inline-size: var(--spectrum-alias-workflow-icon-size, …);
  }
}
```

On an engine without native nesting, the unknown `& { … }` block is discarded and the rule becomes `.spectrum-Icon--sizeS { }`. No size is applied, so the SVG (a `viewBox` with no intrinsic dimensions) resolves its width to **100% of its container**. Live confirmation from an affected host — the rule serialized via CSSOM:

```js
// [...document.styleSheets].flatMap(s => [...s.cssRules])
//   .find(r => r.selectorText?.includes("spectrum-Icon--sizeS")).cssText
".spectrum-Icon--sizeS { }"                       // ← empty on Chromium 99
getComputedStyle(iconSvg).inlineSize              // ← "403px" (== container width)
```

## Minimal reproduction

Self-contained, no build. The right card applies the `3.47.2` rule **exactly as a non-nesting parser retains it**, so it reproduces the bug in any browser. Open the same markup under a real sub-112 engine (e.g. an Adobe CEP panel) and the *unmodified* nested rule fails the same way.

<details><summary><code>repro.html</code></summary>

```html
<style>
  .stage { width: 340px; height: 200px; border: 1px solid #ccc; display: flex;
           align-items: center; justify-content: center; overflow: hidden; }
  .spectrum-Icon { fill: currentColor; display: inline-block; }
  --icon: 18px;
  /* 3.47.1 — flat */
  .flat.spectrum-Icon--sizeS, .flat.spectrum-Icon--sizeS svg {
    block-size: 18px; inline-size: 18px;
  }
  /* 3.47.2 as a pre-112 engine parses it: the nested block is dropped → empty */
  .oldparse.spectrum-Icon--sizeS { }
</style>

<p>3.47.1 (flat) — correct ~18px:</p>
<div class="stage">
  <svg class="flat spectrum-Icon spectrum-Icon--sizeS" viewBox="0 0 36 36">
    <path d="M31.7,4.3a7.176,7.176,0,0,0-10.148,0c-.385.386-4.264,4.222-5.351,5.309a8.307,8.307,0,0,1,3.743.607c.519-.52,3.568-3.526,3.783-3.741a4.1,4.1,0,0,1,5.8,5.8L22.408,19.39a4.617,4.617,0,0,1-3.372,1.3,3.953,3.953,0,0,1-2.7-1.109,4.154,4.154,0,0,1-1.241-1.626,2.067,2.067,0,0,0-.428.318l-1.635,1.712a7.144,7.144,0,0,0,1.226,1.673c2.8,2.8,7.875,2.364,10.677-.438L31.7,14.452A7.174,7.174,0,0,0,31.7,4.3Z"/>
